{title: 099 - God Will Take Care of You}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #099 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 99}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Be not dismayed whate'er betide, God will take care [F7]of you;
[F7]Beneath [Bb]His wings of love abide, God will take care of you.
[Bb/F]God will take care [F7]of you, Through every [Bb]day, o'er [Eb]all the way;
[Bb]He will take care [F7]of you, God will take care of [Bb]you.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb]God will take care of you,
[Eb]through every [Dm]day, o'er [Eb]all the way;
[Bb/F]he will take care of you,
[Bb]God will take care of you.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Through days of toil when heart doth [F7]fail,
[F7]God [Bb]will take care of you;
[Bb/F]when dangers [F7]fierce [Bb]your path [Eb]assail,
[Bb]God will [F7]take care of you.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]All you may need he will provide,
[F7]God [Bb]will take care of you;
[Bb/F]nothing [F7]you ask [Bb]will be [Eb/Bb]denied,
[Bb]God will [F7]take care of you.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]No matter what may be the [F7]test,
[F7]God [Bb]will take care of you;
[Bb/F]lean, weary [F7]one, [Bb]upon [Eb]his breast,
[Bb]God will [F7]take care of you.
{end_of_verse}
